- The ID from the CHIS...
- The ID from the CHIS...

255
00:15:14.568 --> 00:15:16.570
Sorry. boss. great minds.

256
00:15:16.605 --> 00:15:19.366
So. the CHIS who gave us
Turner's name and address?

257
00:15:19.401 --> 00:15:20.643
We need to get him in

258
00:15:20.678 --> 00:15:22.576
to confirm or deny ID
on the Suspect.

259
00:15:22.611 --> 00:15:24.095
I've been on it all day. ma'am.

260
00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:25.510
Handler's lost contact.

261
00:15:25.545 --> 00:15:27.167
He reckons the CHIS
has bottled it.

262
00:15:27.202 --> 00:15:29.307
Christ sake.

263
00:15:29.342 --> 00:15:31.413
Sorry. Chris.
maybe have one more go please?

264
00:15:31.447 --> 00:15:32.724
Boss.

265
00:15:37.695 --> 00:15:40.525
Clearly Turner's
not what we expected.

266
00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:42.458
if that's even his name.

267
00:15:42.493 --> 00:15:44.978
Custody's asked the HCP
to carry out

268
00:15:45.013 --> 00:15:47.394
an initial mental state
examination to make sure

269
00:15:47.429 --> 00:15:49.707
he's got the capacity
to face an interview.

270
00:15:49.741 --> 00:15:51.329
Not just an interview.

271
00:15:51.364 --> 00:15:53.400
A person with learning
difficulties is more likely

272
00:15:53.435 --> 00:15:55.540
to be the victim of crime
than the perpetrator.

273
00:15:55.575 --> 00:15:57.163
You wonder
if he's got the capacity

274
00:15:57.197 --> 00:15:59.268
to carry out a murder
in the first place.

275
00:15:59.303 --> 00:16:01.512
There's always been
two theories.

276
00:16:01.546 --> 00:16:03.169
A hit.

277
00:16:03.203 --> 00:16:06.551
I agree. Kate. he's not our man.

278
00:16:06.586 --> 00:16:10.245
A stalker slash obsessed fan.

279
00:16:10.279 --> 00:16:12.454
That's by far
the more credible theory.

280
00:16:14.421 --> 00:16:16.527
All right.
I'll get right back to you.

281
00:16:19.426 --> 00:16:21.118
Sarge. Front Desk called up.

282
00:16:21.152 --> 00:16:22.533
There's an officer
asking for you.

283
00:16:22.567 --> 00:16:24.638
Won't say what about.
Won't even give a name.

284
00:16:24.673 --> 00:16:26.192
It's late.

285
00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:31.197
Fine. I'll deal with it
on my way out.

286
00:16:40.344 --> 00:16:41.586
Steve Arnott.

287
00:16:41.621 --> 00:16:43.036
Farida?

288
00:16:43.071 --> 00:16:44.658
I'd rather not give my name.

289
00:16:44.693 --> 00:16:46.695
I can appreciate why
that might be but. sorry.

290
00:16:46.729 --> 00:16:48.110
if you're still at Polk Avenue.

291
00:16:48.145 --> 00:16:49.387
AC-3 have jurisdiction now.

292
00:16:49.422 --> 00:16:51.320
And you should contact them.

293
00:16:52.701 --> 00:16:54.220
I'm on the Hill.

294
00:16:55.773 --> 00:16:57.740
Murder Investigation Team.

295
00:17:04.506 --> 00:17:06.059
Wait there.

296
00:17:20.625 --> 00:17:22.386
Can I get you a tea
or coffee or anything?

297
00:17:22.420 --> 00:17:23.904
No thanks.

298
00:17:40.128 --> 00:17:41.543
The rate of unsolved crimes

299
00:17:41.577 --> 00:17:43.476
is proving to be a nightmare.

300
00:17:43.510 --> 00:17:45.823
But it helps the public
to realise that we don't have

301
00:17:45.857 --> 00:17:47.687
the resources
to investigate burglaries.

302
00:17:47.721 --> 00:17:49.620
With any luck they'll stop
reporting them.

303
00:17:49.654 --> 00:17:51.242
the figures will look better.

304
00:17:52.243 --> 00:17:55.177
- Ted.
- Ma'am.

305
00:17:55.212 --> 00:17:57.248
Apologies. ma'am.
I just saw you booked

306
00:17:57.283 --> 00:17:58.836
the conference room there.

307
00:17:58.870 --> 00:18:00.389
My office must have cocked up.

308
00:18:00.424 --> 00:18:01.770
I never got the invitation.

309
00:18:01.804 --> 00:18:03.668
No cock-up.

310
00:18:03.703 --> 00:18:05.843
Sorry. Ted. you're not
on the list this time.

311
00:18:07.638 --> 00:18:10.848
I accepted the disciplinary
action. ma'am.

312
00:18:10.882 --> 00:18:13.126
This matter is now closed.

313
00:18:13.161 --> 00:18:16.509
You lead an anticorruption unit.

314
00:18:16.543 --> 00:18:17.889
There's plenty think
you're lucky

315
00:18:17.924 --> 00:18:19.926
not to have been removed.

316
00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:21.824
Best keep your head down. Ted.

317
00:18:40.222 --> 00:18:41.465
Got a few minutes. gaffer?

318
00:18:41.499 --> 00:18:43.846
Be my guest. son. Be my guest.

319
00:18:46.746 --> 00:18:49.266
Last night I took a statement
from Officer J.

320
00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:51.337
Who was working
at Polk Avenue in 2017

321
00:18:51.371 --> 00:18:52.797
when we investigated
DCI Roz Huntley.

322
00:18:52.821 --> 00:18:54.512
Mmm-hmm.

323
00:18:54.547 --> 00:18:56.697
Officer J. expressed concerns
regarding the professional

324
00:18:56.721 --> 00:18:58.620
conduct of DCI Joanne Davidson.

325
00:18:58.654 --> 00:19:01.001
an SIO on the Murder
Investigation Team

326
00:19:01.036 --> 00:19:03.418
based at Hillside Lane.

327
00:19:03.452 --> 00:19:05.627
Hillside Lane. yeah.
everybody's talking

328
00:19:05.661 --> 00:19:07.594
about this breakthrough
they've made a suspect

329
00:19:07.629 --> 00:19:09.700
- in custody for Vella.
- Yes. sir.

330
00:19:09.734 --> 00:19:12.220
DCI Davidson was posted
to the Hill a year ago.

331
00:19:12.254 --> 00:19:14.222
one month after
Gail Vella's murder.

332
00:19:14.256 --> 00:19:15.682
And She took over
from the original SIO

333
00:19:15.706 --> 00:19:17.294
leading the inquiry.

334
00:19:17.328 --> 00:19:20.814
As you know. sir.
Gail Vella drove home late

335
00:19:20.849 --> 00:19:22.264
on the evening of September 10th

336
00:19:22.299 --> 00:19:24.197
in a dark grey Peugeot 108

337
00:19:24.232 --> 00:19:26.234
which she parked outside
her house in Kingsgate

338
00:19:26.268 --> 00:19:28.822
and was shot dead as she
got out of the vehicle.

339
00:19:28.857 --> 00:19:31.618
At postmortem.
the pathologist concluded

340
00:19:31.653 --> 00:19:33.379
the muzzle of the firearm
had been pressed

341
00:19:33.413 --> 00:19:35.864
against the back of the skull
at the moment of discharge.

342
00:19:35.898 --> 00:19:37.762
Hard-contact technique
to minimise

343
00:19:37.797 --> 00:19:40.455
the spread of sound.
powder and blood.

344
00:19:40.489 --> 00:19:42.433
According to Officer J.
the suspect appears to lack

345
00:19:42.457 --> 00:19:43.872
the capacity
to carry out a murder

346
00:19:43.906 --> 00:19:46.219
that's still unsolved
after over a year.

347
00:19:46.254 --> 00:19:47.772
She also alleges DCI Davidson

348
00:19:47.807 --> 00:19:49.740
unnecessarily diverted
and delayed the operation

349
00:19:49.774 --> 00:19:51.362
to arrest the suspect.

350
00:19:51.397 --> 00:19:54.054
And any previous criticisms
of Davidson on record?

351
00:19:54.089 --> 00:19:55.918
None I've found so far. sir.

352
00:20:00.509 --> 00:20:03.754
I'd like to covertly approach
current members of her team.

353
00:20:08.931 --> 00:20:10.588
Wee Chloe. she's seems to be

354
00:20:10.623 --> 00:20:12.625
getting on really well
out there. doesn't she.

355
00:20:12.659 --> 00:20:14.420
what do you say son?

356
00:20:14.454 --> 00:20:16.318
She's good. sir.

357
00:20:21.634 --> 00:20:23.014
We really can't be sure

358
00:20:23.049 --> 00:20:24.844
about the loyalty
of some of these people.

359
00:20:24.878 --> 00:20:26.432
They could banjax
the whole thing.

360
00:20:26.466 --> 00:20:28.537
Sir. regardless
of the personnel involved.

361
00:20:28.572 --> 00:20:30.436
Vella's still
the highest-profile inquiry

362
00:20:30.470 --> 00:20:31.816
engaging this force.

363
00:20:31.851 --> 00:20:33.991
And Officer J.
Didn't go to AC-3 or AC-9.

364
00:20:34.025 --> 00:20:35.648
She came to AC-12
because she believes

365
00:20:35.682 --> 00:20:38.375
we'll do right by her.

366
00:20:38.409 --> 00:20:40.963
She backed the right horse
there. didn't she son.

367
00:20:40.998 --> 00:20:42.493
But I'm gonna need
a hell of a lot more

368
00:20:42.517 --> 00:20:44.657
before I can authorise
a formal inquiry.

369
00:20:44.691 --> 00:20:46.969
- Sir...
- Houl yer whisht.

370
00:20:47.004 --> 00:20:49.558
I need more.

371
00:20:49.593 --> 00:20:50.870
Sir.

372
00:21:12.823 --> 00:21:14.376
- All right?
- Yeah.

373
00:21:14.411 --> 00:21:15.791
- It's great to see you.
- You too.

374
00:21:15.826 --> 00:21:17.079
I got you one. Hope that's okay.

375
00:21:17.103 --> 00:21:18.484
I'm on the clock.

376
00:21:18.518 --> 00:21:20.106
No. great. I appreciate you

377
00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:21.763
making the time.

378
00:21:21.797 --> 00:21:23.558
I should be calling you "ma'am".

379
00:21:23.592 --> 00:21:26.526
Strictly speaking
but I'll let you off.

380
00:21:26.561 --> 00:21:29.529
So. how can I help you. Steve?

381
00:21:29.564 --> 00:21:31.013
Strictly off the record.

382
00:21:31.048 --> 00:21:33.119
I've reached the end
of the line in anticorruption.

383
00:21:33.153 --> 00:21:34.638
About time.

384
00:21:34.672 --> 00:21:36.502
It's no disrespect
to the Gaffer.

385
00:21:36.536 --> 00:21:39.436
I've stuck it out.
I'm bored. mate.

386
00:21:39.470 --> 00:21:40.747
I'm ready for a new challenge.

387
00:21:40.782 --> 00:21:44.095
Well. we can always
use good people.

388
00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:46.684
Cheers. I appreciate it.

389
00:21:48.134 --> 00:21:50.930
Sorry. I should get back.

390
00:21:52.207 --> 00:21:54.796
But maybe do a drink one night?

391
00:21:55.935 --> 00:21:58.662
- Um...
- Luke and I have split up.

392
00:21:58.696 --> 00:22:00.457
No. it's just...

393
00:22:00.491 --> 00:22:02.044
If we're gonna be
working together.

394
00:22:03.425 --> 00:22:04.668
You really have been working

395
00:22:04.702 --> 00:22:07.636
Anticorruption too long
ain't you.

396
00:22:08.879 --> 00:22:10.708
Good to see you.

397
00:22:27.207 --> 00:22:29.520
DI Fleming. MIT.

398
00:22:32.178 --> 00:22:33.938
Thanks ma'am.

399
00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:37.746
...number of Newspaper
and Magazine clippings

400
00:22:37.770 --> 00:22:40.428
containing images of Gail Vella.

401
00:22:40.462 --> 00:22:42.153
- Morning. Kate.
- Boss.

402
00:22:42.188 --> 00:22:43.821
- All right. Chris.
- All right. ma'am.

403
00:22:43.845 --> 00:22:45.650
I was just saying
there's a number of newspaper

404
00:22:45.674 --> 00:22:47.573
and magazine cuttings

405
00:22:47.607 --> 00:22:50.541
containing images of Gail Vella.

406
00:22:50.576 --> 00:22:51.922
Significant.

407
00:22:51.956 --> 00:22:54.580
Abundant fingerprints
and DNA deposits.

408
00:22:54.614 --> 00:22:55.857
And the prints appear to relate

409
00:22:55.891 --> 00:22:57.652
to two individuals only.

410
00:22:57.686 --> 00:23:00.586
One of who is the suspect
we've got in custody.

411
00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:01.932
Okay.

412
00:23:01.966 --> 00:23:05.245
The search team detected signs
of forced entry.

413
00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:07.524
Our AFOs smashed
the front door in.

414
00:23:07.558 --> 00:23:10.009
The damage is
on the inside of the door.

415
00:23:10.043 --> 00:23:12.805
The markings match the damage
to the back of this chair.

416
00:23:12.839 --> 00:23:14.531
Any estimate
on when this alleged

417
00:23:14.565 --> 00:23:17.430
- forced entry happened?
- No.

418
00:23:17.465 --> 00:23:19.087
It's Farida.
Okay if I take this?

419
00:23:19.121 --> 00:23:20.606
Sure.

420
00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:24.851
Hey. Farida...

421
00:23:24.886 --> 00:23:26.508
Possibly the chair was jammed up

422
00:23:26.543 --> 00:23:28.175
against the front door to
prevent someone breaking in.

423
00:23:28.199 --> 00:23:29.580
Like Chris said.

424
00:23:29.615 --> 00:23:31.168
that could have happened
anytime.

425
00:23:31.202 --> 00:23:32.963
Well. the place
is well maintained.

426
00:23:32.997 --> 00:23:34.250
It's unlikely the damage
would have gone

427
00:23:34.274 --> 00:23:35.655
unrepaired for long.

428
00:23:35.690 --> 00:23:38.209
Unlikely but not impossible.

429
00:23:38.244 --> 00:23:39.659
Good news.

430
00:23:39.694 --> 00:23:42.075
HCP has okayed the suspect
for interview.

431
00:23:42.110 --> 00:23:43.836
Great.

432
00:23:57.574 --> 00:23:59.265
Have a seat.

433
00:24:04.719 --> 00:24:06.134
We'll be with you the whole time

434
00:24:06.168 --> 00:24:07.860
and if you get confused
by anything

435
00:24:07.894 --> 00:24:09.482
it's okay to tell us.

436
00:24:33.368 --> 00:24:35.311
That's just
the tape recorder starting.

437
00:24:35.335 --> 00:24:38.028
it won't last long.

438
00:24:38.062 --> 00:24:40.996
Murder Investigation Team
interview of Suspect A

439
00:24:41.031 --> 00:24:43.551
by Detective Chief
Inspector Davidson

440
00:24:43.585 --> 00:24:45.345
and Detective Sergeant Lomax

441
00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:47.071
in the presence
of the Suspect's Solicitor

442
00:24:47.106 --> 00:24:48.935
and Appropriate Adult.

443
00:24:48.970 --> 00:24:51.006
You do not have to say anything.

444
00:24:51.041 --> 00:24:52.974
It may harm your defence
if you do not mention

445
00:24:53.008 --> 00:24:55.804
when questioned something
you later rely on in court.

446
00:24:55.839 --> 00:24:58.151
Anything you do say
may be used in evidence.

447
00:24:58.186 --> 00:24:59.774
Do you understand?

448
00:24:59.808 --> 00:25:01.223
Yes.

449
00:25:01.258 --> 00:25:03.053
What's your name?

450
00:25:04.951 --> 00:25:06.643
If I may?

451
00:25:06.677 --> 00:25:08.172
My client's informed me
that under the strain

452
00:25:08.196 --> 00:25:10.992
